Target Problem (your task):

\begin{lemma}\label{lem:reduce-to-connected}
Let $\mathcal{A}\rev{(G,T,\omega,\mathcal{F})}$ be any algorithm for {\sc Planar Multiway Cut} with a given set $\rev{\mathcal{F}}$ of $k$ terminal faces that always outputs a \rev{multiway cut of $(G,T,\omega)$}, but is only guaranteed to find an \rev{minimum multiway cut} if for all minimum multiway cuts $C$ to the instance it holds that $C^*$ is connected. Let $T(n,k)$ be a monotone function that describes the running time of $\mathcal{A}$ on instances with $n$ vertices and $k$ terminal faces. Then {\sc Planar Multiway Cut} can be solved in $O(2^{\OO(k)} T(n,k) \mathrm{poly}(n))$ time.
